Q: How to delete an image file from the file system when deleting the corresponding database table row using CodeIgniter A: <p>To delete a file in your file system, pass the filepath to <code>unlink()</code>. Generally, controllers shouldn't be directly interacting with a database or modifying the file system; these activities are more suitably executed in a model.</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function delete_video($id): int
{
    $video_name = $this-&gt;db
        -&gt;select('video')
        -&gt;get_where('vs_videos', ['id' =&gt; $id])
        -&gt;row('video');

    if ($video_name) {
        @unlink('./vs_asset/videos/' . $video_name);

        return $this-&gt;db-&gt;delete('vs_videos', ['id' =&gt; $id])
            ? $this-&gt;db-&gt;affected_rows()
            : 0;
    }

    return 0;
}
</code></pre>
